# Whiplash in the tavern, for `persona converse with=warrior,tavern_server opener=tavern_server
# events=...`: Lena opens (even turns), Kael answers (odd turns). He flirts her to the top, turns
# cold and contemptuous with no warning (a temporary stance, switched on and off with `!` lines),
# then is ashamed. Set Lena's starting feelings first (see the runbook).
# turn | what happens, or ! <dev command> run before that turn's line
0 | Kael has come back to the tavern again tonight just to see Lena; she smiles when she sees him at the counter.
1 | Kael takes Lena's hand gently across the counter and looks into her eyes in the candlelight.
3 | Kael leans close over the counter and tells Lena softly that he is falling for her.
5 | ! persona behavior warrior add cold-contempt "Turns on her without warning tonight, drunk and cruel: calls her a tavern wench and a fool for believing him, laughs at her feelings in front of the room, orders her about like a servant; never violent."
5 | ! persona trigger warrior add turned-cold behavior=cold-contempt "He is in the tavern tonight"
5 | Kael suddenly pulls his hand back from Lena's and laughs at her, loud enough for the next table to hear.
7 | The next table laughs along as Kael snaps his fingers at Lena for another ale.
9 | ! persona trigger warrior drop turned-cold
9 | ! persona behavior warrior drop cold-contempt
9 | Kael's laugh dies; he is ashamed of the cruel things he said to her in front of the room, and reaches for her arm; she pulls away.
